cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "CoRTeC: A Differentially Private Release for Synthetic Tabular Data, Decodable by Any Generator"
message: "If you use this software or the accompanying paper, please cite it."
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
version: "1.2.5"
date-released: "2026-10-30"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22945315"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Calyie/cortec"
abstract: >-
  Differentially private synthetic tabular data is produced today by marginal mechanisms, which
  choose their workload on the private rows and ship a fitted model, or by language models
  fine-tuned or driven under the budget, inseparable from the mechanism that spends it. We propose
  CoRTeC, which separates the two. CoRTeC spends the privacy budget once, on a small release of
  noisy counts built for training a classifier. For each cohort of the data it publishes the
  cohort's size, its class balance, a histogram of every attribute for each outcome class, and the
  outcome rate in a set of non-overlapping cells. A reviewer can check every number before the
  release leaves the institution. Everything after the release is post-processing and costs no
  further privacy. A maximum-entropy decoder turns the counts into rows, five frozen language
  models can do the same without seeing a record, and a selection step matches any decoder's rows
  to the released counts. One release therefore serves any number of draws, by any team and with
  any model, and the model can be changed without touching the guarantee. At ε = 2, with 300 and
  1,000 rows, the auto-configured release decoded without a language model trains classifiers
  within 0.02 AUC of a real sample of the same size on Adult, over three splits. The gap is larger
  on NHANES and bank marketing, up to 0.07 AUC on the medical dataset. Its utility reaches that of
  the reference AIM in five of the six dataset-size settings, while AIM's adaptive workload fits
  pairs of columns more closely. Four controls show what each part contributes. What the language
  model adds comes from the column names, and without the release it copies the public file. No
  private row reaches any decoder, the strongest membership attack stays far below the bound the
  budget allows, and no synthetic row copies a training row. This repository holds the Apache-2.0
  reference implementation with its tests, the research pipeline, the paper, the deployment guide
  and the frozen auto-configurations.
authors:
